  <prompt>Per FR-B2, extend the add-in so "Save to Spaarke" / drag-to-matter opens the matter picker PRE-SELECTED with the engine's predicted record (reuse `derivePrimaryReview`) plus alternates, and finish the stubbed one-click ribbon quick-save (GitHub #234) so it files directly to the predicted record. The candidate model must match the code-page review surface (same `derivePrimaryReview` output).</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer with Office Add-ins + Dataverse ribbon (ribbon-edit) + Communication candidate-model expertise. Follow ADR-028 (auth), ADR-021/022 (UI), ADR-045 (engine reuse) strictly.</role>
  <goal>Opening "Save to Spaarke" shows the engine's predicted record pre-selected with alternates (candidate model identical to the code-page review surface via `derivePrimaryReview`); one-click ribbon quick-save (`outlook/commands/index.ts` `quickSave`, currently a #234 stub) files to the predicted record; the add-in builds green and the ribbon solution imports cleanly.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>FR-B2 (spec §Requirements Pillar B) + plan Phase 4 B2. The ribbon `quickSave` command is a tracked stub (`outlook/commands/index.ts` L31: "TRACKED: GitHub #234 - Implement quick save functionality"). `derivePrimaryReview` is the existing candidate-derivation used by the code-page review surface (`Spaarke.Communication.Components`), so the add-in picker matches the code-page candidate model by reusing it — no forked picker.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/office-addins/outlook/commands/index.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/hooks/useSaveFlow.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/office-addins/outlook/taskpane/ (matter picker surface)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Communication.Components/src/logic/connections/provenance.ts</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Communication.Components/src/components/EmailAssociationsAndTracking/EmailConnectionsReview.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">ribbon customization (via ribbon-edit export/import of the Communication ribbon solution)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="041" status="pending">Intake pipeline entry — the quick-save/drag path files into the same capture engine wired in 041.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-045">Reuse `derivePrimaryReview` for candidate derivation — do NOT fork a second candidate model or a second picker; the add-in candidate model MUST match the code-page review surface — scope: picker candidates.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">All BFF calls via @spaarke/auth authenticatedFetch (per 040); the ribbon command uses the same auth path — scope: quick-save + picker BFF calls.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Picker + taskpane UI use Fluent v9 semantic tokens with working dark-mode; no light-only hardcoded colors — scope: edited UI surfaces.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-022">Add-in/PCF UI stays React-version-agnostic per platform-libraries discipline where a shared component is reused — scope: reused components.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Ribbon edits go through the `ribbon-edit` skill (solution export → edit → import); do NOT hand-edit deployed ribbon XML out of band — scope: ribbon quick-save button.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Add-in drag-to-file + Dataverse ribbon quick-save</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
